    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0312" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.011/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>
                            <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1914.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to herewith enclose a
                    copy and translation of a letter from the Minister for Foreign Affairs in which
                    the Dominican Government pledges itself to abandon its old vicious system of
                    imprisoning people without submitting same prisoners to any tribunal. The
                    Legation has earnestly labored to secure this reform, the meaning of which need
                    not be dwelt upon. In this connection I desire to inform the Department that the
                    Constitutional Convention will be urged to incorporate in the organic law of its
                    country the right of habeas corpus.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James M. Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d223-a1.xml" xpointer="d223-a1"/>
            </div>
